# What the daemon is handed on every build of either image.
#
# This file is not `.gitignore` and is not generated from it: `.git` belongs
# here and not there, and a generated file would hide the one line somebody has
# to think about. What the two must agree on is the direction — anything large
# that git ignores is something a build should not be shipping either, and the
# drift between them is what put 3.3 GB in front of a 20 MB source tree.
#
# TestTheBuildContextIsSource (dockerfile_test.go) walks the tree under these
# rules and fails over a threshold, because a context that grows back makes
# every build slower and produces no error at all.

# Runtime state, never an input to a build.
data/
apps/
logs/
tmp/
.env
*.db

# Build outputs. internal/spa/dist is rebuilt from the frontend stage and
# deleted by the backend stage before the copy, so shipping the local one costs
# 25 MB to be overwritten.
bin/
# What `go build .` leaves at the root, which .gitignore already drops.
/toft
/dist/
web/dist/
internal/spa/dist/

# Dependency trees. Both are reinstalled inside the image from the lockfiles.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
tests/e2e/.venv/

# Scratch. .dev/ is this box's TMPDIR for Go builds (docs/operations.md), so it
# is not merely large — it is written *while a build is running*, which makes
# the context nondeterministic as well as slow.
.dev/
tests/e2e/reports/
**/*.log

# History. Nothing in either build reads a revision.
.git
# Claude Code's skills and agent worktrees — whole checkouts of the tree.
.claude/
